<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Northern War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1700–1721</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Northern War (1700–1721) was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and a coalition led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. After early Swedish successes, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden">Charles XII</a>'s defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-poltava">Poltava</a> in 1709 broke Swedish power, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nystad">Treaty of Nystad</a> in 1721 transferred Baltic provinces to Russia, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> and establishing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> as a great power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-northern-war.jpg" alt="Great Northern War" width="320" height="364" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Imonoz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_Northern_War_Collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
